    <briefdescription>
<para>Evaluates the effective startup security class after HSM initialization. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This maps policy intent (<computeroutput><ref refid="namespacethemis_1_1security_1a71f1c3c981a929aa3c6f0abbbff2e908" kindref="member">resolveHSMStartupPolicy</ref></computeroutput>) and the observed runtime provider state (real PKCS#11 vs. stub) into a hard gate decision.</para>
<para>Failure/edge cases:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>If a stub provider is active without explicit insecure opt-in, startup must be blocked.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If PKCS#11 was configured but runtime still fell back to stub, startup must be blocked unless explicit insecure opt-in is present. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
